data.content:
It works. Here's the full program targeting `net11.0`:

**Program.cs**
```csharp
using System.Text.Json;

var person = new Person("Alice", 30);

var options = new JsonSerializerOptions
{
    PropertyNamingPolicy = JsonNamingPolicy.PascalCase
};

Console.WriteLine(JsonSerializer.Serialize(person, options));

public record Person(string name, int age);
```

**Output:**
```json
{"Name":"Alice","Age":30}
```

`JsonNamingPolicy.PascalCase` is new in .NET 11 — it converts the record's lowercase positional-parameter properties (`name`, `age`) to PascalCase (`Name`, `Age`) in the serialized JSON. No custom policy needed.
